#: includes/admin/documentation.php:107
msgid "User Roles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:108
msgid "Besides the Volunteer role, the plugin offers two roles for delegating day-to-day work without handing out full Administrator access:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:111
msgid "Role"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:112
msgid "Can do"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:116
#: includes/helpers.php:127
msgid "Volunteer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:117
msgid "Sign up for and cancel shifts, edit their own profile. No access to wp-admin beyond that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:120
#: includes/helpers.php:201
msgid "Shift Manager"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:121
msgid "Create, edit, and delete shifts and departments, and manage volunteers (assign them to shifts, edit their department links). Cannot access Import or Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:124
#: includes/helpers.php:205
msgid "Volunteer Manager"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:125
msgid "Manage volunteers (edit their department links) and send announcements. Cannot create, edit, or delete shifts, and cannot access Import or Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:128
msgid "Administrator"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:129
msgid "Full access to everything, including Import and Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:133
msgid "Assign a role under Users → All Users → edit the user → Role."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:134
msgid "Important:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:134
msgid "a WordPress account can only have one role at a time through that Role dropdown — picking a new role there replaces the old one, it does not add to it. So switching an Administrator to Shift Manager or Volunteer Manager removes their Administrator access; only do this for accounts that should not have full admin access. The one exception is the Volunteer role: use the \"Grant volunteer role\" / \"Remove role\" buttons on the Volunteers page instead of the Role dropdown to add or remove it without disturbing whatever other role the account already has — for example, to let a Shift Manager or Volunteer Manager also show up on the Volunteers page itself, so they can be assigned to a shift or receive department-targeted announcements."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:137
msgid "Departments (Manager → Departments) group shifts, can be nested under a parent, and each carries a color used for its badge on shift cards and in the overview. \"Hide from volunteers\" removes a department from the frontend filter and labels; a shift disappears for volunteers only when every department it belongs to is hidden (shifts someone already signed up for are never hidden). Color, parent, visibility, and description can also be changed via Quick Edit in the department list, and the shift list itself can be filtered and sorted by department."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:139
msgid "Shift Overview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:140
msgid "The shift overview (Shifts → Overview) is split into four tabs, each showing only the filters relevant to it:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:142
msgid "registered volunteers, upcoming shifts, and open spots split into required (below a shift's minimum) and optional (up to the maximum)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:143
msgid "Cards"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:143
msgid "the shift cards, with filters for upcoming/past/all, department, volunteer, and date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:144
msgid "a flat, export-style table; the \"Add volunteer\" button assigns someone without leaving the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:145
msgid "Timeline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:145
msgid "a per-volunteer Gantt chart. Drag a shift's bar to move or resize it (with an Undo after saving), or use the Edit Shift modal for exact times. Unfilled slots show as red (below minimum) or grey (optional) bars, which can be toggled off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:148
msgid "Volunteer List & Badges"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:149
msgid "The Volunteers page (Shifts → Volunteers) lists all volunteer accounts and shows badges next to each name to indicate how the account was created or its current status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:152
msgid "Badge"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:153
#: includes/admin/documentation.php:225
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:158
msgid "Created by an admin without an email address. Cannot log in and receives no notifications."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:161
#: includes/admin/volunteer-list.php:405
msgid "Manual"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:162
msgid "Added by an admin via the dashboard form or the \"Grant volunteer role\" function. Never auto-deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:165
#: includes/admin/volunteer-list.php:399
msgid "Unverified"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:166
msgid "Registered via the public form but has not yet clicked the magic login link. The account is auto-deleted once the link expires (~24 h). The badge disappears as soon as the link is clicked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:169
#: includes/admin/volunteer-list.php:402
msgid "Social"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:170
msgid "Registered or linked via Nextend Social Login (e.g. Google, Facebook). Requires the Nextend Social Login plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:173
msgid "(no badge)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:174
msgid "Self-registered via the public form and verified by clicking the magic link, or registered before the badge system was introduced (version 0.9.8)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:178
msgid "A volunteer can have multiple badges at the same time (e.g. Manual + Social)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:181
msgid "The Send Announcement page (Shifts → Send Announcement) lets you send a custom email to volunteers. Available recipient options:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:183
msgid "Subscribed only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:183
msgid "Volunteers who opted in to announcements (default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:184
msgid "Every volunteer with an email address, regardless of opt-in status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:185
msgid "Split volunteers by whether they currently have an upcoming shift assigned — useful for nudging people who haven't signed up yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:186
msgid "Only the volunteers assigned to a selected shift or department. A live recipient count is shown once you pick one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:187
msgid "Every volunteer linked to a department (Volunteers page → Edit), regardless of shift history or opt-in status — useful for announcing new shifts to a department before anyone has signed up for one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:188
msgid "Individual volunteer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:188
msgid "Click \"Email\" on any volunteer row to open the form pre-filled for that person."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:190
msgid "The From name and From email can be overridden per send. Use {first_name} and {last_name} as personalisation placeholders, and {shifts} to list each recipient's own upcoming shifts. HTML formatting is supported — the live preview below the form renders the email as it will appear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:191
msgid "A PDF can optionally be attached — it will be sent with every email in that announcement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:192
msgid "Every sent announcement is recorded in the collapsible Send History table on the same page. The table can be filtered by typing and sorted by clicking column headers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:193
msgid "Offline volunteers (no email address) are excluded from all announcement sending. Volunteers can opt out under their profile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:195
msgid "Reminder & Notification Emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:196
msgid "Volunteers are emailed when they are assigned to or removed from a shift, and again as a reminder a configurable number of days before it starts (Settings → Communication → Reminders — leave the days field empty to switch reminders off). All three messages use a rich-text editor and share placeholders such as {first}, {last}, {title}, {start}, {end}, {desc}, {department}, {department_desc}, and {days}. Each shift can override the sender through a linked WordPress user and/or a manual organizer name and email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:198
msgid "E-mail Design"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:199
msgid "Settings → Communication → E-mail design styles the shared wrapper around every plugin email: a header color, a header title and subtitle shown next to the site logo, a rich-text footer, and — under advanced — custom CSS applied to all emails. The filters below are for changes that go beyond these options."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:201
msgid "Email Template Customization"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:202
msgid "All plugin emails use a shared HTML wrapper so registration links, assignment confirmations, cancellations, and announcements have a consistent look."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:203
msgid "Integrators can customize or fully replace this wrapper in theme code or a small companion plugin using WordPress filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:205
msgid "Adjust template variables such as heading, preheader, site name, or footer text before the final HTML is generated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:206
msgid "Modify only the inner email body HTML while keeping the default wrapper."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:207
msgid "Replace the complete final HTML output if you need a fully custom branded layout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:209
msgid "Example: add this in your theme’s functions.php or a small custom plugin to change the footer text of all EventAdmin emails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:214
msgid "Use a custom plugin instead of editing EventAdmin directly if you want your changes to survive plugin updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:216
msgid "Automatic Cleanup of Unverified Accounts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:217
msgid "A daily background job automatically deletes volunteer accounts that were registered via the public form but whose magic login link expired without ever being clicked. Accounts are only deleted if they have no shift assignments and are not marked as manually added."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:218
msgid "A log of automatically deleted accounts (up to the last 100) is shown at the bottom of the Volunteers page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:220
msgid "Public \"Open Positions\" Overview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:221
msgid "The [eventadmin_open_positions] shortcode shows visitors who are not logged in where volunteers are still needed, grouped by department. Only departments with unfilled slots in upcoming shifts are listed. Put it on a public recruitment page, next to the [eventadmin_register] form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:224
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:230
msgid "\"summary\" (default): one line per department with its open-slot count. \"list\": every open shift, grouped under its department."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:234
msgid "Comma-separated department slugs to limit the output to. Default: all visible departments."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:238
msgid "\"0\" hides the \"We still need volunteers in:\" intro line (summary style only)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:242
msgid "\"1\" also includes shifts whose slots are already filled (list style only)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:246
msgid "\"0\" also includes shifts that have already ended. Default: past shifts are hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:251
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:253
msgid "Do volunteers need an account?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:254
msgid "Yes, they must be logged in to view and join shifts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:256
msgid "How can I assign volunteers manually?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:257
msgid "In the admin dashboard under “Volunteer Overview” for each shift via form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:259
msgid "What happens when shifts are full?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:260
msgid "By default, full shifts are hidden on the volunteer page. You can optionally show them in a separate read-only section by enabling \"Show full shifts to volunteers\" under Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:262
msgid "What is the minimum volunteers field for?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:263
msgid "You can set a minimum number of volunteers per shift. The admin dashboard will highlight shifts that have not reached the minimum with an understaffing warning. This is informational only – no signup rules are enforced based on the minimum."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:265
msgid "Can visitors see where help is needed before registering?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:266
msgid "Yes. Put the [eventadmin_open_positions] shortcode on any public page. It lists every department that still has unfilled slots, needs no login, and by default shows a compact summary — add style=\"list\" for the individual open shifts."
msgstr ""

